# Installed as /usr/share/lintian/overrides/phpr-cli (via
# debian/phpr-cli.install); justifies the tags that stem from upstream
# (php-rust) being a statically-linked Rust binary.
#
# "curl": the binary embeds no C code from curl. The HTTP client is the
# pure-Rust ureq crate (with rustls); lintian matches on curl-related
# protocol strings. Static Rust crates cannot be replaced by a system
# libcurl at packaging level.
phpr-cli: embedded-library curl [usr/bin/phpr]
# "libyaml": same class — the unsafe-libyaml Rust crate (a transitive
# dependency via serde_yaml/mysql parsing), not the C libyaml; nothing
# is linked against the system libyaml.
phpr-cli: embedded-library libyaml [usr/bin/phpr]
